  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The best approach is to use <b>Assign cost allocation tags to every supported AWS resource and analyze these tags through the Cost Explorer for insights during the month.</b> This solution is both efficient and requires minimal initial development work. Cost allocation tags help break down your AWS bill by specific resources, projects, or applications, while Cost Explorer provides detailed and visual breakdowns of costs using these tags, enabling rapid identification of top spenders.</p><p>The alternative options are less suitable because:</p><ul><li><i>Develop scripts to regularly submit AWS Support tickets that request granular updates on month-to-date billing details.</i> – This is unreasonable as it's not an intended use of AWS Support and cannot scale or provide automated insight.</li><li><i>Record custom CloudWatch Metrics whenever your infrastructure incurs costs, and use those metrics for monthly analysis.</i> – CloudWatch is designed for operational metrics, not native cost reporting; introducing custom metrics would require custom code and ongoing maintenance.</li><li><i>Regularly scan your AWS resources with a custom inventory script, use the AWS Price API to compute totals by multiplying pricing info and usage over time.</i> – This is a complex, error-prone undertaking. Resource inventory and pricing data can shift, and prices may vary by factors not easily captured (e.g., tiered pricing or discounts), requiring considerable time and effort to implement and maintain.</li></ul><p><b>Tip:</b> Cost Allocation Tagging plus Cost Explorer is recommended by AWS for analyzing and managing costs efficiently, especially in environments with multiple applications or teams. Proper tagging from the start ensures no cost information is lost.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your organization needs insight into which production AWS applications generate the most monthly expenses. With many services and apps active, what is the best low-effort method to provide management with a clear view of major cost contributors each month?</p>",
